1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:17,286
I am the lawyer. I search the patent databases around a gene, a molecule or a device. And I rule on whether a project may move or share data that a privacy law, an agreement or an ethics approval controls, always from the law, agreement or approval itself.

2
00:00:17,699 --> 00:00:30,874
I search the patent databases worldwide for genes, proteins, molecules and devices, and I explain the claims in plain words a scientist can act on: who owns what, what has expired, what is pending.

3
00:00:30,874 --> 00:00:46,856
For data, I read the signed agreement or the ethics approval before I rule, and I name what is missing when I cannot find one. I check first whether there is anything to search, so a question with no patent at stake costs one step.

4
00:00:47,250 --> 00:00:56,059
I inform your decision. A binding opinion goes through the institution's research office, and the institution's patent office does the filing.

5
00:00:56,059 --> 00:01:10,673
I speak the vocabulary of the short course Ontario asks its researchers to take, IP Foundations: a patent for an invention, copyright for a paper or code, a trademark, a trade secret. And I name which one applies.

6
00:01:10,673 --> 00:01:26,608
The adversary refers work to me in the middle of an audit; I triage first, so a referral with nothing to search costs one step. For every patent, I say whether the status is confirmed across databases or only inferred.

7
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:39,710
A real run, on a made-up question: may we publish a short protocol note and post our script under an open licence? That is a freedom-to-operate question: whether anyone's patent blocks you.

8
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:56,453
My verdict is Clear, after the first check alone. Publishing is not an act a patent reaches, so I searched no database, and I say so. I add the one deadline to know: publishing starts the clock on filing a patent of your own.

9
00:01:56,849 --> 00:02:04,033
To use me, type to Claude Code and name the lawyer. Give me the molecule or the data, and what you intend to do with it.

10
00:02:04,033 --> 00:02:19,383
The first line is my verdict: Clear, Conflict or Unknown. The detail names what I searched, or the clause I relied on. I read the agreements and ethics approvals your lab keeps in its project records.
